    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "So you're saying Miller's plan is just bad policy? That seems like a huge leap. People argue that intervention is necessary to protect working families from being crushed by price spikes. \n\nIf you're saying Smith is the \"proven\" choice, aren't you just ignoring the risks of deregulation and the potential for huge inequality? It feels like you've already picked a winner here.",
